kettle — third-party attributions

This product depends on and/or adapts ideas from the following projects:

* Alacritty (alacritty_terminal, vte) — Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/alacritty/alacritty
  kettle uses alacritty_terminal for its VT parser, grid and scrollback model.

* WezTerm (portable-pty) — MIT
  https://github.com/wez/wezterm
  kettle uses portable-pty for cross-platform PTY / Windows ConPTY support, and
  its image-protocol implementations were used as a reference.

* cosmic-text / glyphon — MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Text shaping, font fallback and GPU glyph atlas.

* resvg / usvg — Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  https://github.com/linebender/resvg
  The media worker renders SVG with resvg and usvg, which draw with
  tiny-skia (BSD-3-Clause) and shape text with harfrust (MIT) and skrifa
  (MIT OR Apache-2.0). Kettle's SVG admission mirrors resvg's allocation
  geometry; the code is original.

* Merman, merman-core, merman-render, dugong, dugong-graphlib and manatee
  0.8.0 - MIT OR Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/Latias94/merman
  The media worker uses its SVG and Cytoscape layout adapters with package
  defaults disabled. Native diagram measurements use Kettle's SVG font database.

* roughr-merman 0.12.3 - MIT
  https://github.com/Latias94/merman
  Deterministic sketch primitives used by the pinned diagram renderer.

* pulldown-cmark 0.13.4 - MIT
  https://github.com/pulldown-cmark/pulldown-cmark
  CommonMark parsing for the Mermaid fences of a Markdown diagram gallery,
  with its HTML writer and command line disabled.

* objc2, block2 and the objc2 framework crates (objc2-av-foundation,
  objc2-core-media, objc2-core-graphics, objc2-core-foundation,
  objc2-foundation) — MIT, and Zlib OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  https://github.com/madsmtm/objc2
  On macOS the media worker calls AVFoundation through these bindings.
  The decoders themselves are Apple's, part of the operating system.

* FFmpeg — not distributed
  When the user has installed ffmpeg and ffprobe, the media worker runs
  them as separate programs to decode video. Kettle neither bundles nor
  links them; their licenses are those of the user's own build.

* Contour — Apache-2.0
  Reference for the Sixel parser state machine.

* kitty — GPL-3.0 (specification consulted, no GPL code copied)
  https://github.com/kovidgoyal/kitty
  kettle-vt's kitty graphics protocol implementation
  (`kettle-vt/src/kitty.rs`, `placeholder.rs`) follows kitty's
  published spec: the image transfer / placement / animation /
  Unicode-placeholder model, chunk-reassembly semantics, and
  relative-placement chain are all kitty's design. The
  implementation is original code in Rust; we cite the
  specification author for the design.

* Terminator — GPL-3.0 (UX convention consulted, no GPL code copied)
  https://github.com/gnome-terminator/terminator
  kettle's tabs / splits / broadcast-input UX + default keybinds
  (`terminatorlib/config.py`, `terminatorlib/terminator.py`) are
  Terminator's convention: `Ctrl+Shift+O` for top/bottom split,
  `Ctrl+Shift+E` for left/right split, the `broadcast_all`
  group-input semantics scoped per-tab. The implementation is
  original Rust code; we cite the upstream as the convention's
  origin.

* Ghostty — MIT
  https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty
  kettle's `key = value` config syntax, the `theme` key behavior,
  and the `unfocused-split-opacity` default 0.7 all follow
  Ghostty's convention. The implementation is original; the
  surface (key names, parsing rules, defaults) matches
  Ghostty's so a user's Ghostty config drops in unchanged.

Bundled assets:

* JetBrains Mono Nerd Font — SIL Open Font License 1.1
  See assets/fonts/OFL.txt
  The regular face is also embedded in the media worker as its default SVG
  font; explicit per-job outline faces may supplement it. Font tests derive
  synthetic renamed outline fixtures in memory from this asset, retaining
  its copyright and license records. They test coverage and collection-face
  selection, not authentic non-Latin typography.

* iTerm2-Color-Schemes (Ghostty theme set) — MIT
  See assets/themes/LICENSE
  https://github.com/mbadolato/iTerm2-Color-Schemes

* Fira Sans 4.301 - SIL Open Font License 1.1
  Digitized data copyright 2012-2018, The Mozilla Foundation and Telefonica S.A.,
  bBox Type GmbH and Carrois Corporate GbR, with Reserved Font Name "Fira".
  See assets/fonts/fira-sans/OFL.txt and README.md for exact source provenance.
  The media worker embeds matching regular, bold, italic and bold italic
  outlines for proportional diagram labels.
  Monospace inline code reuses the JetBrains Mono Nerd Font asset listed
  above; diagram layout and final SVG shaping use the same per-job database.

* Merman / Mermaid createText conventions -- MIT OR Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/Latias94/merman
  Native formatted-label measurement follows Merman 0.8.0's row baselines,
  whitespace boundaries, literal word spans and line-break conventions.
  Kettle's bounded implementation is original.

